{"title":"2013 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two bees start at the same spot and fly at the same rate in the following directions. Bee <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot north, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot east, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot upwards, and then continues to repeat this pattern. Bee <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> travels <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot south, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> foot west, and then continues to repeat this pattern. In what directions are the bees traveling when they are exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet away from each other?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/9/189cd94747f9414d8c87bef0168013a057ec033f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } A\\ \\text{east, } B\\ \\text{west} \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } A\\ \\text{north, } B\\ \\text{south} \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } A\\ \\text{north, } B\\ \\text{west} \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } A\\ \\text{up, } B\\ \\text{south} \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } A\\ \\text{up, } B\\ \\text{west}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"878\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let A and B begin at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/9/4e9f36b13a11a14accae8e072c0cf34d69267bb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,0,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"59\" height=\"20\" />. In <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> steps, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> will have done his route twice, ending up at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/4/3d4d0787f258358551930ba1f3dbdab59fa1a9a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,2,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> will have done his route three times, ending at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/8/228200a2fef126868a5e7112d56ab857b682a7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3,-3,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. Their distance is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9e20713213e444a2c9e445b314b53e319648052.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(2+3)^2+(2+3)^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{54} &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"302\" height=\"32\" />. We now move forward one step at a time until they are ten feet away:\n</p><p>7 steps: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> moves north to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b0280aebf8b4eb06b4eb9b0f8376eef9cec787a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> moves south to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/9/86969448d0e1a3f29502f71281e6b58a98b37146.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-3,-4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/0/0b0fa5c3dce98fc569b1f99473ac83d37133acbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(2+3)^2+(3+4)^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{78} &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"302\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>8 steps: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> moves east to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/4/3743da5af2793e9e268234fa98ec06299c8b1485.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3,3,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> moves west to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42925b4c064fd3e0347c12b5cabb1fe5305e0d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-4,-4,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />, distance of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/7/fd759cd630154b9aa33342ceaafbd97ec253c056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{(3+4)^2+(3+4)^2+2^2}=\\sqrt{102}&gt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"311\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>Thus they reach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> feet away when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> is moving east and B is moving west, between moves 7 and 8. Thus the answer is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/e/35e8ea2d16518197b5113002b8c0c7da6c311a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"41\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf